# Signal Fish Godot dev container - local environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env*` is git-ignored (this file is the committed exception). The dev
# container loads `.env.local` into the container environment at container
# create time via `runArgs: ["--env-file", ...]` in
# `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json`, so values exist only in the process
# environment. Committed MCP configuration files (`.mcp.json`,
# `opencode.json`, the `~/.codex/config.toml` managed block) reference these
# variable NAMES only - never paste a secret into a config file.
# See `.devcontainer/README.md` ("MCP servers") for the full wiring.

# --- GitHub MCP server (github-mcp-server) ---------------------------------
# Fine-grained personal access token. Read-only is the default; grant
# additional scopes (issues/pull requests write) only if you flip
# GITHUB_READ_ONLY to 0.
# https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
GITHUB_MCP_PAT=

# --- Context7 (library documentation lookup; optional) ---------------------
# Works without a key at anonymous rate limits; a key raises the limits.
# https://context7.com/dashboard
CONTEXT7_API_KEY=

# --- Optional overrides -----------------------------------------------------
# Set to 0 to let the GitHub MCP server mutate repos, issues, and pull
# requests. Default: 1 (read-only).
#GITHUB_READ_ONLY=1
# Comma-separated GitHub MCP toolsets. Default: the server's default set.
#GITHUB_TOOLSETS=context,repos,issues,pull_requests

# --- Not MCP ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Z.ai provider credentials used by terminal agents (e.g. nanocoder
# providers); consumed directly by those CLIs, not by MCP servers.
#Z_AI_API_KEY=
#Z_AI_MODE=
